# SHUIMUMUU Tarot Backend - Agentic AI Development Guidelines

This file defines the project-specific rules, constraints, and workflows for any Agentic AI Coding Assistant working on this codebase. These rules MUST be read and followed strictly during every task.

---

## 📌 Core Rule: Version Synchronization (版號同步規則)

Every time you modify the stylesheet CSS or layout elements and bump the cache-buster version suffix in `static/index.html` (e.g., `style.css?v=2.3.x`):
1. **You MUST synchronously update the foot note version number** at the bottom of the page in `static/index.html` (inside `<p class="footer-note">v2.3.x</p>`) to the exact same version number (e.g., `v2.3.x`).
2. Keep the version suffix in `static/index.html` and the footer note perfectly in sync so the user and developer always see the correct, updated release version.

---

## 🎨 Layout & UI Design Guidelines (排版與設計準則)

### 1. Music Banner Layout (.music-banner)
- **Compact & Centered**: Keep the banner width compact (`width: fit-content; max-width: 100%; margin: 0 auto;`) and items centered (`justify-content: center;`). Never let the banner stretch fully across wide panels leaving empty gaps.
- **Deformation Prevention**: Always set `flex-shrink: 0;` on the circular jellyfish logo wrapper (`.music-logo-wrapper`) and SVG icons (`.music-icon`) to absolutely prevent the circle or SVG from getting squeezed/deformed into ellipses.
- **Responsive Stack**: On viewports ≤ 300px (like high zoom or extremely narrow windows), stack the banner elements vertically (`flex-direction: column; text-align: center;`) for clean, gorgeous, and bug-free mobile responsiveness.

### 2. Sidebar Button Spacing (.left-toggle-btn)
- Keep the spacing between sidebar emojis/text to exactly `3.5px` (`margin-bottom: 3.5px;` on `.btn-emoji`). This ensures the emojis and vertical text are perfectly proportioned.

### 3. Desktop Single Row
- Ensure the music banner stays as a single horizontal line (`flex-wrap: nowrap;` by default) on standard desktop sidebar panels (width 280px).

---

## 🚀 Git & Deployment Workflow (Git 與部署工作流程)

- After finishing any edits and making sure they build/render perfectly:
  1. Stage all modifications: `git add .`
  2. Commit with a descriptive message: `git commit -m "..."`
  3. Push to main: `git push origin main`
- Pushing to GitHub automatically triggers the Render platform Auto-Deploy pipeline (takes ~2 minutes to sync). Always notify the user that their cloud version is being compiled and will sync shortly!
